/* @catalog — generated by `npm run catalog:generate`; do not edit by hand.
 * Internal
 *   Classes: Storage
 *   Functions: mutation, code, wav, file, create, prepared, existingProject, appendProject, cancelPublication
 *   Constants: actor, other
 *   Variables: harness
 * Tests
 *   - private storage requires separate configured bucket, and real byte metadata precedes durable PUT
 *   - upload lost response recovers exact bytes without a second PUT; same key changed payload is refused
 *   - failed cleanup retains exact storage evidence and same intent retry completes it
 *   - explicit publish allocates fixed IDs then commits complete catalog graph after copy checkpoint
 *   - unknown copied acknowledgement is reconciled at original target with no second object or graph
 *   - unconfirmed copy retains fixed identities and cannot be silently resent by retry or worker restart
 *   - role loss after copied bytes prevents publication and keeps copy evidence for admin recovery
 *   - hidden publication needs no delivery gate, and the parent hides independently public tracks
 *   - confirmed cleanup permits replacement while old cleanup replay cannot delete the new object
 *   - manual artwork has private exact-version preview and explicit selection; deleted candidates cannot preview
 *   - private artwork rechecks role after bytes arrive, withholding late response after revocation
 *   - append adds only new members, preserves existing metadata and protected old tracks, and same-album reuse is no replacement
 *   - append keeps the target Album disc order and imported tracks store no Disc Number
 *   - append revalidates reviewed Album after storage copy and refuses concurrent catalog edits
 *   - verified byte candidates bind SHA to current object version and identify only matching manifest slots
 *   - append rejects hidden draft into public target without changing draft visibility
 *   - legacy ready defaults tolerate reference touches, and hidden Artist Album can be appended privately
 *   - embedded cover becomes a private unselected candidate, while its tags never overwrite the saved draft
 *   - shutdown after one bounded copy checkpoints it and admits no next cover copy or final publication
 *   - publication grant expiry after a copy retains its checkpoint and stops later copies and final catalog commit
 *   - publication rechecks grant between destination HEAD and new copy dispatch
 *   - expired publication is explicitly cancelled, cleaned and reapproved without losing the previous identities
 *   - concurrent reused Artist correction returns to manual review and a newly reviewed candidate may publish
 *   - current administrator can cancel and clean after the initiating admin loses permission and flags roll back
 *   - unknown sent copy retains cancelled source pins until the exact late object can be cleaned by any current admin
 *   - cancelled cleanup reconciles failed or lost DELETE responses without copying or deleting another object
 *   - publication cancellation rejects stale revisions, another approval, UUID collisions, active leases and committed graphs
 *   - all 200 staged objects from supported 100 tagged files can be cleaned at the ordinary receipt limit
 *   - staged cleanup takeover reuses the exact original UUID and revision after the first administrator loses role
 *   - publication cancellation and staged cleanup remain admissible when ordinary writes have exhausted receipts
 *   - an expired-lease worker cannot checkpoint or publish its late result after cancellation and a new approval
 *   - cancelled cleanup retains a replaced canonical version without deleting an unapproved identity
 *   - sixteen approvals preserve bounded history and reject the seventeenth before new identity admission while recovery remains available
 * @end-catalog */

